; Claiming the rest. Winning 42, Ch. 12, Hand 32 trick 4 (S-0143-c): the bidder
; trumps the 5-4 with the 1-0 and lays his hand down; and Ch. 3 (S-0054-a).
; Claim, in our words: a player to play may show his hand and claim every trick
; left when one order of his tiles takes them all, whatever the hidden layout
; and whatever the other three play.
; Reading: (lay-down), from any seat that is to play, following or leading. It
; claims tricks, not the bid: in Hand 32 the bidder is already set when he
; claims (lay-down.silas, the bidder's claim of his bid, does not hold there).

(query (roles (chair c))
  (out)
  (pattern
    (viewer c)
    (lay-down)))
